// NEGATIVE TEST -- `macro_rules!` in INVOCATION position gets the same sentence
// as in item position (N3-14).
//
// tests/reject/macro_rules.pd pins the declaration `macro_rules! name { … }`.
// This is the other place a reader arriving from Rust types the name, and it
// used to answer "Unknown macro 'macro_rules'" -- which reads as a typo in the
// NAME when the problem is the SYSTEM. One refusal, two positions, and the
// sentence names what this language has rather than what it lacks
// (src/macros/mod.rs, `unknown_macro`).
//
// The control for over-refusal is in tests/03_macros.pd: `macro_rules` as an
// ORDINARY IDENTIFIER still compiles and runs, because what is refused is the
// name followed by `!`, not the spelling.
fn main() {
    print_int(macro_rules!(4));
}
